Writer: cells of an imported DOCX/RTF table with the same attributes share one cell format.

The DOCX/RTF table import sets borders, widths and shading through the cell UNO objects, so every cell got a cell
format of its own (SwTableBox::ClaimFrameFormat): about 0.5 KB each with its attribute set and name. A table made
in Writer shares one format between equal cells, and SwTableBox::ClaimFrameFormat gives a cell its own format again
as soon as it is changed. After a table is converted, HstShareEqualTableBoxFormats (new hsttableboxformats.cxx)
moves every cell whose format has the same attribute set and parent as an earlier cell's onto that format
(SwTableBox::ChgFrameFormat deletes the unused one). Cells with a number format, value or formula keep their
own format, since the core finds such a cell through its format. At most 64 distinct formats per table are compared, so the
pass stays linear in the number of cells.

Hook: sw/source/writerfilter/dmapper/DomainMapperTableHandler.cxx (one call after the table is converted),
sw/Library_sw.mk; logic in sw/inc/hsttableboxformats.hxx, sw/source/core/table/hsttableboxformats.cxx.
Test: CppunitTest_sw_writerfilter_dmapper testHstEqualCellsShareOneFormat (equal cells share, a changed cell gets
its own format back); DOCX round trips of the upstream sw/qa files are unchanged.
